"sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000095017023054855/msft-20230930.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10Q_2023-03-31__financial_statements__0092", "ticker": "MSFT", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q3 FY2023", "period_end": "2023-03-31", "section": "financial_statements", "score": 0.719, "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-Q Q3 FY2023", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000095017023014423/msft-20230331.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10Q_2022-12-31__mdna__0006", "ticker": "MSFT", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q2 FY2023", "period_end": "2022-12-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.8967, "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-Q Q2 FY2023", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000156459023000733/msft-10q_20221231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10Q_2022-12-31__financial_statements__0095", "ticker": "MSFT", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q2 FY2023", "period_end": "2022-12-31", "section": "financial_statements", "score": 0.7192, "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-Q Q2 FY2023", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000156459023000733/msft-10q_20221231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2022-06-30__mdna__0004", "ticker": "MSFT", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2022", "period_end": "2022-06-30", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.8848, "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-K FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000156459022026876/msft-10k_20220630.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10Q_2022-03-31__financial_statements__0098", "ticker": "MSFT", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q3 FY2022", "period_end": "2022-03-31", "section": "financial_statements", "score": 0.7193, "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-Q Q3 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000156459022015675/msft-10q_20220331.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 40, "dropped_candidates": 175, "token_estimate": 31964, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "Microsoft reports its financial performance in three segments: Productivity and Business Processes, Intelligent Cloud, and More Personal Computing [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0003]. In the 10-K for fiscal 2025 (ended June 30, 2025), it says the segments give management a comprehensive financial view of its key businesses and a framework for allocating resources [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0003]. Productivity and Business Processes is described as productivity, communication, and information services across a variety of devices and platforms, while Intelligent Cloud is public, private, and hybrid server products and cloud services [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0004][MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0007]. More Personal Computing is described as products and services that put customers at the center of the experience with Microsoft's technology [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0010]. In August 2024 Microsoft announced changes to segment composition, most notably bringing the commercial components of Microsoft 365 together in Productivity and Business Processes [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0003]. The Q2 fiscal 2026 10-Q (ended December 31, 2025) describes the same three segments [MSFT_10Q_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0089].", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "MSFT", "company": "Microsoft Corporation", "findings": [{"point": "Microsoft operates and reports using three segments (Productivity and Business Processes, Intelligent Cloud, More Personal Computing), which it says give management a comprehensive financial view and a framework for resource allocation (10-K, fiscal 2025, ended June 30, 2025).", "citations": ["MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0003"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Productivity and Business Processes primarily comprises Microsoft 365 Commercial, Microsoft 365 Consumer, LinkedIn, and Dynamics products and cloud services (10-K, fiscal 2025, ended June 30, 2025).", "citations": ["MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0004"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Intelligent Cloud primarily comprises server products and cloud services (including Azure) and enterprise and partner services; More Personal Computing primarily comprises Windows and Devices, Gaming, and Search and news advertising (10-K, fiscal 2025, ended June 30, 2025).", "citations": ["MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0007", "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0010"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": {"columns": ["Segment", "How Microsoft describes it (10-K, fiscal 2025, ended June 30, 2025)"], "rows": [["Productivity and Business Processes", "Productivity, communication, and information services across devices and platforms [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0003]"], ["Intelligent Cloud", "Public, private, and hybrid server products and cloud services for business and developers [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0007]"], ["More Personal Computing", "Products and services putting customers at the center of the experience [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0010]"]]}, "citations": [{"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0003", "claim": "Three segments; they provide management a comprehensive financial view and resource allocation framework; August 2024 composition change", "quote": "We operate our business and report our financial performance using three segments"}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0004", "claim": "Productivity and Business Processes segment description and components", "quote": "products and services in our portfolio of productivity, communication, and information services, spanning a variety of devices and platforms"}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0007", "claim": "Intelligent Cloud segment description and components", "quote": "public, private, and hybrid server products and cloud services that power modern business and developers"}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0010", "claim": "More Personal Computing segment description and components", "quote": "products and services that put customers at the center of the experience with our technology"}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10Q_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0089", "claim": "Same three segments reported in Q2 fiscal 2026 10-Q", "quote": "Productivity and Business Processes, Intelligent Cloud, and More Personal Computing"}], "coverage": {"companies_used": [{"ticker": "MSFT", "forms": ["10-K", "10-Q"], "fiscal_periods": ["FY2025", "Q2 FY2026"]}], "companies_missing": [], "data_as_of": "Q2 FY2026, ended December 31, 2025 (10-Q filed 2026-01-28)"}, "gaps": ["Segment descriptions are drawn mainly from the fiscal 2025 10-K and the Q2 fiscal 2026 10-Q; a detailed comparison of wording changes across all earlier filings was not performed."], "confidence": "high", "confidence_reason": "Multiple chunks from the fiscal 2025 10-K and the latest 10-Q directly state the segment names and descriptions consistently.", "next_questions": ["How did revenue and operating income compare across the three segments in fiscal 2025?", "What changed in the segment composition announced in August 2024?", "What drove Intelligent Cloud revenue growth in fiscal 2025?"], "refusal": null}, "citations_resolved": [{"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0003", "claim": "Three segments; they provide management a comprehensive financial view and resource allocation framework; August 2024 composition change", "quote": "We operate our business and report our financial performance using three segments", "ticker": "MSFT", "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-K FY2025", "section_title": "Business", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-06-30", "filing_date": "2025-07-30", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000095017025100235/msft-20250630.htm", "truncated": false, "quote_mismatch": false, "valid": true, "kind": "chunk"}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0004", "claim": "Productivity 